{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/56720-4-example-ciphers","id":56720,"title":"4 Example Ciphers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-24T07:04:45-08:00","id":56720,"title":"4 Example Ciphers","content":"Here are the Interlocks I came up with for my party's Ciphers. I went with a suggestion I found here on the forum to make an Interlock between the 1st and 4th Keys, so there are 4 Interlocks per Cipher. Not posting the final secret because the players don't want to tell each other and they know about these forums. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Cipher - Chaos and Discord - Destroyer<br /> <br /> Key 1 Merciless Gunman<br /> Key 2 Special Someone<br /> Key 3 Unperson<br /> Key 4 Combustion</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Interlock 1 Merciless Gunman &amp; Special Someone <br /> Who Needs to Die</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Wits + Firearms</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Choose a target as with Special Someone and fire your gun into the air. You won't find the target, but your bullet might. Repeated use of this in a scene will break Cover, a bullet falling from the sky and randomly striking someone is plausible, but a stream of them is not.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Dramatic Failure - Apparently you need to die, take 1 + Weapon Damage Lethal. <br /> Failure - Who knows where that bullet went. <br /> Success - If there is no cover between your bullet and the target, they take successes + Weapon Damage Lethal. If there is cover the bullet will go around it they take Weapon Damage Lethal. If the target is completely cut off, but the bullet can punch through a window or wall it will reducing the damage appropriately. <br /> Exceptional Success - Do successes + weapon damage lethal even with cover, punching through objects still reduces this damage.<br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Interlock 2 Special Someone &amp; Unperson<br /> Charlatan</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Manipulation + Subterfuge - Composure</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">This causes the target's identity to be replaced instead of erased. Choose a general type of person. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Dramatic Failure - The demon loses his identity and everyone else believes he is the type of person named. The player must immediately roll compromise for breaking cover. <br /> Failure - No Effect, -1 cumulative penalty for each successive attempt to remove or alter the target's identity. <br /> Success - The target is identified as the type of person that was specified instead of their own identity for the rest of the scene. They cannot establish specific details such as a name at all. <br /> Exceptional Success - The target also believes that they are the type of person specified. But they may not be able to pull it off because their skills haven't changed.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Interlock 3 Unperson &amp; Combustion<br /> What is That!?</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Wits + Subterfuge - Composure</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">This causes the target's identity to be replaced with that of a horrible flaming monster.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Dramatic Failure - The demon loses his identity and everyone believes he is a horrible flaming monster. The player must immediately roll compromise for breaking cover. <br /> Failure - No Effect, -1 cumulative penalty for each successive attempt to remove or alter the target's identity. <br /> Success - The target loses his identity and everyone that sees him believes he is a horrible flaming monster for the rest of the scene. <br /> Exceptional Success - If the demon wishes it, the target actually bursts into flames taking successes in lethal damage.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Interlock 4 Combustion &amp; Merciless Gunman<br /> Flaming Bullets</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Wits + Firearms</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The demon's firearm is enhanced to set the bullets on fire as they are fired.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Dramatic Failure - The bullets are set on fire, right now! The demon takes the gun's damage in lethal and the gun is ruined as the magazine explodes. <br /> Failure - No Effect. <br /> Success - The gun does +2 fire damage for the rest of the scene. <br /> Exceptional Success - The gun does +4 fire damage for the rest of the scene and can set flammable objects on fire.</span></span><br /> <br /> Cipher - Stop the Killing - Destroyer who became a Pacifist<br /> <br /> Key 1 Merciless Gunman<br /> Key 2 Just Bruised<br /> Key 3 Check Backdrop<br /> Key 4 On the Mend<br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Interlock 1 Merciless Gunman &amp; Just Bruised<br /> Merciful Gunman</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Wits + Firearms</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">In Down &amp; Dirty combat:<br /> Dramatic Failure - 1 target dies and combat proceeds with the opponents enraged and less likely to surrender. <br /> Failure - Gun fails to fire. <br /> Success - The gunman knocks unconscious number of successes plus damage rating of gun. <br /> Exceptional Success - The gunman knocks unconscious a number of opponents equal to his bullets.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Out of Down &amp; Dirty combat: <br /> Success: The attack deals bashing damage with 8 again. The next consciousness roll by the target automatically fails if the attack hit. <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><br /> Interlock 2 Just Bruised &amp; Check Backdrop<br /> Rubber Bullets</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Wits + Firearms</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Dramatic Failure - The combat becomes incredibly lethal. All bashing damage is lethal and all damage ignores armor. <br /> Failure - No Effect. <br /> Success - The combat is less deadly. All damage is reduced from lethal to bashing or aggravated to lethal. <br /> Exceptional Success - The demon can specify any number of targets give their consciousness checks a -2 penalty. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Interlock 3 Check Backdrop &amp; On the Mend<br /> Inspired by Incompetence</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Manipulation + Medicine</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Dramatic Failure - The demon loses a point of willpower and takes 1 lethal damage. <br /> Failure - No Effect. <br /> Success - Any time an attack misses in the next scene the target gains 1 willpower and their worst wound is downgraded 1 level. Aggravated turns to lethal, lethal turns to bashing, and bashing is healed. <br /> Exceptional Success - The wound is healed regardless of severity instead of downgrading. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Interlock 4 On the Mend &amp; Merciless Gunman<br /> Healing Bullet</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Dexterity + Medicine</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-1 cumulative penalty for every time this is used in a scene after the first. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Dramatic Failure - The bullet misses the target and ricochets into the demon doing weapon damage. <br /> Failure - The bullet misses. <br /> Success - The target has 1 point per success + 1 point per weapon damage of their worst level of wound downgraded 1 level. Aggravated turns to lethal, lethal turns to bashing, and bashing is healed. If there are points left over after a level is completely healed, those points are used on the next worst level of damage. For example if a person has 2 aggravated and 3 successes are rolled with an assault rifle, all of their damage is healed. <br /> Exceptional Success - The target and the demon both regain a point of willpower from the impressive healing. </span></span><br /> <br /> Cipher - Everyone should be able to use all knowledge and access the God Machine's Power<br /> <br /> Key 1 Borrowed Expertise<br /> Key 2 Freeze Assets<br /> Key 3 In My Pocket<br /> Key 4 Tools Into Toys<br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Interlock 1 Borrowed Expertise &amp; Freeze Assets<br /> Borrowed Assets</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Manipulation + Academics</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">As Borrowed Expertise, but applies to Merits instead of Skills. <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><br /> Interlock 2 Freeze Assets &amp; In My Pocket<br /> Empty Your Pockets</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Manipulation + Larceny</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Dramatic Failure - The demon's pockets are emptied. He cannot pull anything out of them for the rest of the scene. <br /> Failure - No Effect. <br /> Success - The target cannot find what he is looking for in his pockets no matter how hard he searches. They are empty and the target cannot pull anything out of them for the scene. <br /> Exceptional Success - This also effects any containers the target currently has with him such as his backpack or trunk of his car. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Interlock 3 In My Pocket &amp; Tools Into Toys<br /> Fake Linchpin</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Dexterity + Crafts<br /> The demon touches a Linchpin and tries to pull a fake copy of it out. The fake linchpin will keep the infrastructure running and it will appear to be running normally to an inspection. This can only be attempted once per Linchpin.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Dramatic Failure - The demon exposes himself to the infrastructure and gains the Flagged Condition as well as rolling Compromise. <br /> Failure - No Effect, you cannot try to replace this Linchpin again. <br /> Success - The demon pulls a copy of a Linchpin out of his pockets, but it is not the real linchpin and the infrastructure will no longer function properly if they are switched. <br /> Exceptional Success - If the demon successfully switches the linchpin the infrastructure changes its function. The demon cannot control the function, but it will definitely not be what the God Machine intended <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><br /> Interlock 4 Tools Into Toys &amp; Borrowed Expertise<br /> Are you sure you know how to do that?</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Manipulation + Academics - Skill Being Removed</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Dramatic Failure - The target gets a +3 bonus to all rolls with that skill and the demon loses that skill for the rest of the scene. <br /> Failure - No Effect. <br /> Success - The target reduces their skill by 1 per success, but it cannot go below 0 and they still count as having it for purposes of untrained penalties and can still use specialties. <br /> Exceptional Success - The skill can go below 0 and they cannot use specialties, but they still count as having it for the purposes of untrained penalties.</span></span><br /> <br /> Cipher - Corrupt and control from the shadows<br /> <br /> Key 1 Don't I Know You?<br /> Key 2 Identity Theft<br /> Key 3 Shift Consequence<br /> Key 4 Interference <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><br /> Interlock 1 Don't I Know You? &amp; Identity Theft<br /> I Do Know You</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Manipulation + Empathy</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Dramatic Failure - You look like someone the target dislikes. <br /> Failure - No Effect. <br /> Success - As Identity Theft, but you become a person that your target was expecting to see. Nothing happens to that person, and you may not look or act exactly like them, your new Identity is stolen from the target's mind. <br /> Exceptional Success - Lasts for 24 Hours</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Interlock 2 Identity Theft &amp; Shift Consequence<br /> Meet My Minion</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">You may use Identity Theft and I Do Know You for other people. If they are not willing, subtract their Composure from the roll. Using these on a human reveals your demonic nature and compromises accordingly. <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><br /> Interlock 3 Shift Consequence &amp; Interference<br /> It was Him!</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Manipulation + Occult - Resolve<br /> You can try to shift a new glitch to someone else as a reflexive action as you gain the glitch.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Dramatic Failure - The compromise you just tried to shift gets worse, upgrade the severity of the glitch or roll another compromise if it was catastrophic. <br /> Failure - No Effect. <br /> Success - Move a glitch you just suffered to another person. If it was a permanent glitch it reverts to you after 24 hours. <br /> Exceptional Success - A permanent glitch stays with the target forever. If this was a permanent glitch gained because of increased Primum, you gain another permanent glitch after 24 hours. You can try to shift that one as well, but will continue to gain new glitches until one sticks.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Interlock 4 Interference &amp; Don't I Know You?<br /> Patsy</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Primum</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">You can not only spread out your demonic nature away from yourself with Interference, you can also concentrate it away from yourself on a specific target. You can Spoof other people into detecting as a Demon. Roll Primum, if the target is also Spoofing you need more successes than them, otherwise 1 success is enough to make the target detect as a Demon.</span></span><br /> </span></span><br /> </span></span><br /> </span></span><br /> </span></span><br /> </span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1105-hulsmanm","name":"hulsmanm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T13:01:16-08:00","id":58260,"title":"","content":"So this brings up a question. Conceptually I understand what the final Truth is. But I don't get what it means for the character and the player. Things like &quot;<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#222222\">Chaos and Discord&quot;, What does that mean to the Player? Especcially if they were already just creating chaos? How is the Final truth supposed to focus a Demon's Descent and how is it supposed to be enlightening for the Demon?</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T05:55:20-08:00","id":58647,"title":"","content":"Those aren't the final truths, as I said I didn't post the final truths because some of my players read this forum. Chaos &amp; Discord is what that character's goal for hell is and I put that there so you know why the interlocks do the things that they are doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1105-hulsmanm","name":"hulsmanm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}